From: The412Banner <the412banner@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ws2_32: Report 0 bytes sent for sendto() on a closed socket in DiRT 3 and DiRT Showdown.

DiRT 3 (dirt3_game.exe) and DiRT Showdown (showdown.exe, showdown_avx.exe) close their
motion telemetry UDP socket at the end of a race (and when leaving Joyride) but keep calling
sendto() on it. sendto() fails with WSAENOTSOCK and the game stops with
"sendto failed with error 10038: (null)". The same happens on Windows with telemetry on.

For these executables only, sendto() failing with WSAENOTSOCK now returns 0 (no bytes sent)
with the last error cleared. Other games and every other sendto() result are unchanged.

Same behaviour as DiRTTelemetryErrorFix by RoccoC (MIT), based on the original fix by
Carsten Gottschling: https://github.com/RoccoC/DiRTTelemetryErrorFix

Tested 2026-10-31 on a Retroid Pocket Duo (DroidDeck, DroidDeck-Proton 11-11.9) with the same
rule in a stand-in ws2_32.dll: DiRT Showdown with telemetry on, leaving Joyride no longer shows
the 10038 error and the game exits cleanly.
---
 dlls/ws2_32/socket.c | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+)

--- a/dlls/ws2_32/socket.c
+++ b/dlls/ws2_32/socket.c
@@ -3261,6 +3261,32 @@
                 lpOverlapped, lpCompletionRoutine );
 }
 
+/* DiRT 3 and DiRT Showdown close their motion telemetry UDP socket at the end of a race and keep
+ * calling sendto() on it. The WSAENOTSOCK failure makes them stop with "sendto failed with error
+ * 10038". For these executables only, such a send reports 0 bytes sent instead, as the Windows fix
+ * DiRTTelemetryErrorFix by RoccoC (based on Carsten Gottschling's fix) does. */
+static BOOL ignore_sendto_on_closed_socket(void)
+{
+    static const WCHAR *const games[] = { L"dirt3_game.exe", L"showdown.exe", L"showdown_avx.exe" };
+    static LONG cached = -1;
+    const WCHAR *app, *p;
+    LONG found = 0;
+    unsigned int i;
+
+    if (cached != -1) return cached;
+    app = NtCurrentTeb()->Peb->ProcessParameters->ImagePathName.Buffer;
+    if (app)
+    {
+        if ((p = wcsrchr( app, '\\' ))) app = p + 1;
+        if ((p = wcsrchr( app, '/' ))) app = p + 1;
+        for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(games); i++)
+            if (!wcsicmp( app, games[i] )) found = 1;
+    }
+    if (found) FIXME_(winediag)( "sendto() on a closed socket reports 0 bytes sent for %s.\n", debugstr_w(app) );
+    InterlockedExchange( &cached, found );
+    return found;
+}
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *		sendto		(WS2_32.20)
  */
@@ -3273,7 +3299,14 @@
     wsabuf.buf = (char*) buf;
 
     if ( WS2_sendto(s, &wsabuf, 1, &n, flags, to, tolen, NULL, NULL) == SOCKET_ERROR )
+    {
+        if (GetLastError() == WSAENOTSOCK && ignore_sendto_on_closed_socket())
+        {
+            SetLastError( 0 );
+            return 0;
+        }
         return SOCKET_ERROR;
+    }
     else
         return n;
 }
